From: Ryan Qin <ryqin@google.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:55:04 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 42/43] [3.1.1] [M156] [FedCM] Return early in ShowVerifyingDialog() if
 the view destroys it

Original change's description:
> [FedCM] Return early in ShowVerifyingDialog() if the view destroys it
>
> IdentityDialogController::ShowVerifyingDialog() calls into the account
> selection view, which can dismiss the dialog synchronously. That can
> complete the request and destroy the controller, but the view can still
> report that the dialog was shown, and the controller then used its
> members. Check that the controller is still alive before using them.
>
> Fixed: 574609353
> Change-Id: Iec835fd4d2a6065c35a47f4a7bad34a52fc2f3ad
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8756152
> Reviewed-by: Yi Gu <yigu@chromium.org>
> Commit-Queue: Ryan Qin <ryqin@chromium.org>
> Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1738057}

(cherry picked from commit 8dfc7dce720f57a13f7f171e1e963ec6ac4b7b8a)

